{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"d9b55bab1e2eacfc","name":"card_event_naval_engagement","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Italy/events/card_event_naval_engagement","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"NAVAL ENGAGEMENT","text":"Fully repair all units in your support line. Destroy all units in the enemy support line.","flavorText":"Although the Italian Navy (Regia Marina) was outmatched by the British fleet in the Mediterranean during WWII, there were a few instances where they achieved success. \r\n\r\nIn the Battle of Cape Spartivento in November 1940, Admiral Inigo Campioni led the Italian Navy in a confrontation with the British Mediterranean Fleet. Italian cruisers and destroyers successfully attacked a British convoy bound for North Africa, causing damage to British ships. The Italian Navy managed to escape without significant losses.\r\n\r\nIn the Second Battle of Sirte, which took place in March 1942, the Italian Navy, once again under Admiral Angelo Iachino's command, attacked a convoy of supply ships en route to North Africa. Engaging British warships, the Italian fleet damaged the cruiser HMS Cleopatra and sank the destroyer HMS Kingston.\r\n\r\nHowever, during the Allied Invasion of Sicily in 1943, the Italian Navy was overwhelmed by the superior Allied naval forces. The Italian fleet was largely neutralized, with several ships being captured or scuttled by their own crews to prevent them from falling into enemy hands. This led to the eventual surrender of the Italian Navy to the Allies in September 1943. Subsequently, the Italian fleet was either disarmed or incorporated into Allied naval operations for the remainder of the war.","faction":"Italy","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":9,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_naval_engagement","title":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_naval_engagement_title","SourceString":"NAVAL ENGAGEMENT","LocalizedString":"NAVAL ENGAGEMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Italy","kredits":9,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_naval_engagement_text","SourceString":"Fully repair all units in your support line. Destroy all units in the enemy support line.","LocalizedString":"Fully repair all units in your support line. Destroy all units in the enemy support line."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_naval_engagement_history","SourceString":"Although the Italian Navy (Regia Marina) was outmatched by the British fleet in the Mediterranean during WWII, there were a few instances where they achieved success. \r\n\r\nIn the Battle of Cape Spartivento in November 1940, Admiral Inigo Campioni led the Italian Navy in a confrontation with the British Mediterranean Fleet. Italian cruisers and destroyers successfully attacked a British convoy bound for North Africa, causing damage to British ships. The Italian Navy managed to escape without significant losses.\r\n\r\nIn the Second Battle of Sirte, which took place in March 1942, the Italian Navy, once again under Admiral Angelo Iachino's command, attacked a convoy of supply ships en route to North Africa. Engaging British warships, the Italian fleet damaged the cruiser HMS Cleopatra and sank the destroyer HMS Kingston.\r\n\r\nHowever, during the Allied Invasion of Sicily in 1943, the Italian Navy was overwhelmed by the superior Allied naval forces. The Italian fleet was largely neutralized, with several ships being captured or scuttled by their own crews to prevent them from falling into enemy hands. This led to the eventual surrender of the Italian Navy to the Allies in September 1943. Subsequently, the Italian fleet was either disarmed or incorporated into Allied naval operations for the remainder of the war.","LocalizedString":"Although the Italian Navy (Regia Marina) was outmatched by the British fleet in the Mediterranean during WWII, there were a few instances where they achieved success. \r\n\r\nIn the Battle of Cape Spartivento in November 1940, Admiral Inigo Campioni led the Italian Navy in a confrontation with the British Mediterranean Fleet. Italian cruisers and destroyers successfully attacked a British convoy bound for North Africa, causing damage to British ships. The Italian Navy managed to escape without significant losses.\r\n\r\nIn the Second Battle of Sirte, which took place in March 1942, the Italian Navy, once again under Admiral Angelo Iachino's command, attacked a convoy of supply ships en route to North Africa. Engaging British warships, the Italian fleet damaged the cruiser HMS Cleopatra and sank the destroyer HMS Kingston.\r\n\r\nHowever, during the Allied Invasion of Sicily in 1943, the Italian Navy was overwhelmed by the superior Allied naval forces. The Italian fleet was largely neutralized, with several ships being captured or scuttled by their own crews to prevent them from falling into enemy hands. This led to the eventual surrender of the Italian Navy to the Allies in September 1943. Subsequently, the Italian fleet was either disarmed or incorporated into Allied naval operations for the remainder of the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Naval_Support_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Naval_Support_17.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Italy/Spring2023Candidates/t_italy_naval.t_italy_naval","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Look and Learn","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/NAVAL_ENGAGEMENT.NAVAL_ENGAGEMENT","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":295.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_italy","Key":"card_event_naval_engagement_photo","SourceString":"The Italian cruiser Gorizia firing at British destroyers during the Second Battle of Sirte, 1942.","LocalizedString":"The Italian cruiser Gorizia firing at British destroyers during the Second Battle of Sirte, 1942."},"OnPlayedFromHandVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_OrderAmphibianAssault.BP_OrderAmphibianAssault_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"cardsToDestroy","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_naval_engagement","owner":"card_event_naval_engagement_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable_1","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable_1","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue_1","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_DestroyMultipleCards_qqq","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetCardsInSupportLineBySide_cards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Get_Item","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_FullyHealCard_HealedAmount","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetOppositeSide_oppositeSide","type":"ESideEnum","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Less_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetCardsInSupportLineBySide_cards_1","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Get_Item_1","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue_1","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Less_IntInt_ReturnValue_1","type":"bo